Z||000000||Ali_Gulf_Fiero||12-14-2001||08:52 AM||||If I buy a new engine for my Sport Coupe, and I tell them I need a duke for an '85, which version of the engine do I get?<BR>Will it come with a serpentine belt?<BR>Force balancer?<BR>Bad con rods?<BR>Have they fixed the problems?<BR>Is it old stock, or new castings?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||MR2KLR||12-14-2001||05:02 PM||||you would get one with the OIL filter on the side, V-belts and ready for use with a 300 TBI if you got one for post 87 you would get one with the OIL filter in the pan, DIS, 700 TBI and Serp. belt I don't think either one if bought NEW would have Chevette Rods to chuck through the block  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <BR>Black 88 Coupe: 120 MPH spedo, Aux. gauge pod, 195/55VR14 Potenza RE-71 tires, GT exhaust & ground F/X Soon to have 16" White Beretta GTZ W/ 215/45ZR16's<BR><A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A>||||reg||1
